                <pb facs="0343" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4713: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Magruder</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-27T19:00:00-04:00">July 27, 1931—7
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>18. Your telegram No. 28, July 25, 10 p.m. In place of the message contained in
                    Department’s No. 14, July 3, 2 p.m., please transmit the following to the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I have noted with pleasure that the Portuguese Government has decided to
                            accept the President’s proposal and to postpone for 1 year the
                            collection of the German reparations due to Portugal. It is most
                            encouraging to this Government to see that the Portuguese Government is
                            following the President’s suggestion. The cooperation thus given by the
                            Portuguese Government toward relief and the re-establishment of economic
                            stability and prosperity of the world is gratifying to this
                            Government.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
